A procedure that already uses :TRY/:CATCH and also ends with a legacy
:ERROR handler. mixed_error_handling_families (warning) fires once,
ranged on the :ERROR that introduced the mix; deprecated_keyword fires on
each legacy keyword separately (diag.mixed_error_handling_families
first Flags fence).
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE CountRows;
	:PARAMETERS sRegion;
	:DECLARE nCount;
	:TRY;
		nCount := LSearch("SELECT COUNT(*) FROM ORDERS WHERE REGION = ?", 0,, {sRegion});
	:CATCH;
		nCount := 0;
	:ENDTRY;
	:RETURN nCount;
	:ERROR;
	nCount := -1;
	:RESUME;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE CountRows;
	:PARAMETERS sRegion;
	:DECLARE nCount;

	:TRY;
		nCount := LSearch("SELECT COUNT(*) FROM ORDERS WHERE REGION = ?", 0,, {sRegion});
	:CATCH;
		nCount := 0;
	:ENDTRY;

	:RETURN nCount;
	:ERROR;
		nCount := -1;
	:RESUME;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
10:2-10:8 warning deprecated_keyword: ':ERROR' is legacy error handling. Prefer ':TRY' / ':CATCH' / ':FINALLY'
10:2-10:8 warning mixed_error_handling_families: Legacy ':ERROR'/':RESUME' and structured ':TRY'/':CATCH' are mixed in the same procedure - the legacy handler can intercept errors before ':CATCH' sees them; use one family per procedure
12:2-12:9 warning deprecated_keyword: ':RESUME' is legacy error handling. Prefer ':TRY' / ':CATCH' / ':FINALLY'
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
10:2-10:8 warning deprecated_keyword: ':ERROR' is legacy error handling. Prefer ':TRY' / ':CATCH' / ':FINALLY'
10:2-10:8 warning mixed_error_handling_families: Legacy ':ERROR'/':RESUME' and structured ':TRY'/':CATCH' are mixed in the same procedure - the legacy handler can intercept errors before ':CATCH' sees them; use one family per procedure
12:2-12:9 warning deprecated_keyword: ':RESUME' is legacy error handling. Prefer ':TRY' / ':CATCH' / ':FINALLY'
